**Read:** [Calculus and differential-equation preparation — Strang and Herman, OpenStax](../sources/Calculus-and-Differential-Equations-OpenStax.lingua#r_027WKVM5NG5X84M86TSVRA77J3), Volume 1 chapters on limits, derivatives, integration and applications, then the complete Volume 2 differential-equation chapter; whole volumes for needed mathematical depth; [Chemical Reactor Analysis and Design Fundamentals — Rawlings and Ekerdt](../sources/Chemical-Reactor-Analysis-Rawlings-Ekerdt.lingua#r_7YQAV27Y3J0B537Z6K5HDN8H0A), the complete model, stoichiometric matrix, material/energy balance and computational-appendix foundations; [Graduate Numerical Methods Applied to Chemical Engineering — MIT 10.34](../sources/Graduate-Numerical-Methods-MIT-10-34.lingua#r_1NTDP6EFQGR8HWP34VT9ZJ98DV), the introductory mathematical-model, linear-system and error-analysis preparation.

A function assigns a quantity to a specified state or input; a derivative describes its local rate of change and an integral accumulates it over an interval. If n(t) is an amount in mol, dn/dt has units mol per time. A steady-state balance sets the chosen inventory derivative to zero, not the chemical reaction rate or every internal gradient.

For an original simple decay model dn/dt=−kn with n(0)=n₀, differentiation verifies n(t)=n₀e^(−kt). Integrating the reaction consumption over time gives n₀−n(t), closing the material account. Initial conditions, units and the domain of a rate law are part of this model, not optional decoration attached after solving it.

Several species or thermal variables create coupled equations. A partial derivative holds specified other variables fixed; a Jacobian collects local responses and helps analyze conditioning or stability. A numerical root satisfies equations only within its tolerances; physical constraints, uniqueness, stable states and comparison with observations are further questions.

**Work:** use the complete calculus reading where a tool is unfamiliar. Derive a transient species and energy model from accumulation, verify a limiting analytic solution by differentiation/integration, and explain each variable, condition and constraint. Reuse [Quantitative and technical literacy](../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2) and [Reproducible computational work](../../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ) for units, graphs, sensitivity, discretization and computational checks; the later graduate work deepens the mathematical models through actual chemical cases.

**Continue:** [Infer chemical rates from a defined experiment and test competing mechanisms](../kinetics/Rate-laws-mechanisms-parameters-and-evidence.lingua#r_0YJBZ45WHB3M0N4ZA64MKE4KAE).

